poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Norm Labbe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-05-06T02:01:05.000Z","updated_at":"2023-05-06T02:01:05.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/teVknwjSGXFO5y1rhYoli","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/teVknwjSGXFO5y1rhYoli"}},{"id":"hs1Dva8lwGMdY2LOVykcT","ext":"jpg","post_id":"5k9QuhmBqNUWt0WUgHg2j","description":"Plenty of water on the Rock","caption":"Triple drop on the Rock","poi_name":null,"subject":"Rick Gonzales","author":"Norm Labbe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-05-06T02:03:52.000Z","updated_at":"2023-05-06T02:03:52.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/hs1Dva8lwGMdY2LOVykcT","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/hs1Dva8lwGMdY2LOVykcT"}},{"id":"opft1pGD44hX5pRNoLq96","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Oxhi2tjVm4CdSTJfsa5G8","description":"","caption":"Water from the Essex Chain of Lakes flowing into the Rock","poi_name":null,"subject":"Nelson Miller","author":"Norm Labbe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-05-06T02:05:56.000Z","updated_at":"2023-05-06T02:05:56.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/opft1pGD44hX5pRNoLq96","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/opft1pGD44hX5pRNoLq96"}},{"id":"L4KYyHzWlzgaFZNpdbVvJ","ext":"jpg","post_id":"2iuiohspUbtm1x6zeIq86","description":"Gage reading was 6.4 on the Hudson","caption":"Rock River put-in","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Norm Labbe","poi_id":"108205","photo_date":"2023-05-06T01:54:18.000Z","updated_at":"2023-05-06T01:54:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/L4KYyHzWlzgaFZNpdbVvJ","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/L4KYyHzWlzgaFZNpdbVvJ"}},{"id":"CpOp1ZsriDjO7YsccYUhU","ext":"jpg","post_id":"YLGwH3KMohS7mH6P7flls","description":"Hudson River gage was 6.4 ft. A few more difficult rapids followed this before we reached the Hudson. . ","caption":"On the Cedar River after the Rock river flowed into it. ","poi_name":null,"subject":"Nelson Miller and Derek Snyder","author":"Norm Labbe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-05-06T02:10:15.000Z","updated_at":"2023-05-06T02:10:15.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/CpOp1ZsriDjO7YsccYUhU","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/CpOp1ZsriDjO7YsccYUhU"}}],"detail":{"id":"1391","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Starting at the outlet of Lake Durant the Rock runs through backcountry until it meets the Cedar and then meets the Hudson upstream of the Indian confluence. Expect lots of flat water, beautiful views, and some quality white water. It will grow and grow over the course of the 16 or so miles to the Indian River confluence. You'll want to catch this one within 6-8 hours after a big rain, with the Hudson 6ft and rising.\n\nThe put-in is at the outlet of Lake Durant. And you can take out upstream of the Indian River confluence at the Gooley Club (depending on whether the road is open / how long you are willing to hike) or continue down to North River.\n\nFrom Lake Durant the creek goes into Rock Lake. These first few miles will be scratchy, with a couple beaver dams. Once you arrive at Rock Lake, keep to the left shore - the inlet and outlet are right next to each other, so the flatwater is limited. After Lake Durant the river will pick up and there will be two Class 4 drops to scout before the Cedar confluence. Scout RR and RL respectively. The second is a beautiful three tier drop, but the RL portage is challenging if you decide to walk. At this point the Rock has gained significant volume from several tributaries.\n\nOnce you join the Cedar (comes in from RR in a boggy section) it will be class III with one class IV at an island. You can scout the island rapid from high on RL. You then join the Hudson is class II-III at this point. If you started on the Rock and it was navigable, the Cedar (and the Hudson) will have a big-water feel, though totally manageable.\n\n**Eastern Adirondacks Reaches**\n\n[Ausable, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1238/) [Ausable, W. Branch (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1241/) [Ausable, W. Branch (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1239/) [Balm of Gilead Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2996/)\n\n[Boquet (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1261/) [Boquet (3.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1262/) [Boquet, N. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1264/)[Boquet, S. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1263/)\n\n[Boreas (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1266/) [Branch, The (Boquet trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1441/) [Branch, The (Schroon trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1442/) [Cedar (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1280/)\n\n[Cedar (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1281/) [Cold](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1287/) [Deer Creek (Hudson Trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1184/)[Glen Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1309/)\n\n[Hague Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10876/) [Hudson (0.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10653/) [Hudson (1. Indian River to North River)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1321/) [Hudson (2. North River to Riparius)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1322/)\n\n[Hudson (3. Riparius to the Glen)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1323/) [Indian (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1325/) [John's Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2913/)[La Chute](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1335/)\n\n[Mettawee](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1343/)[Mill Creek (Essex County](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4251/))                    [Mill Creek (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1346/) [North Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4303/)\n\n[Pike Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10886/) [Poultney](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1383/)[Putnam Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4253/) [Raquette (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1385/)\n\n[Rock River](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1391/) [Schroon (North Hudson to Schroon Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1422/) [Schroon (Starbuckville to Riverbank)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1423/)[Schroon (Warrensburg to Thurman Station)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1421/)\n\n[Squaw Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3886/) [Styles Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4281/) [Thirteenth Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1443/) [Trout brook (Schroon trib)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3284/)\n\n[West Mill Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4314/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)**","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":nu